{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 51cb1f6e, F after the failed gate at 43e9b328.\n\n1. Fixture scope: the split, as you propose.\n   a. The Grow cost case stays on the exact retained TEST Room and Site\n      bytes, with the old pins and the old receipt. A cost receipt is a\n      measurement of those bytes. No rebaseline. The case then also\n      shows that a retained definition still runs after F, and rulings\n      0a0286c4 and 23559d21 rest on that.\n   b. The publication case and the failed-claim case use the canonical\n      packet. Each derives its expected text digest from the exact\n      signed child declaration before the archive step, and compares it\n      with the archive at the same Directory position. Keep the\n      retained byte count, the discovery check and the replay check.\n   c. No production archive change, no edit of a signed demo. State in\n      the implementation note which of the nine cases run on retained\n      bytes and which on canonical bytes, in one table.\n\n2. The Worker exit and the missing owner. A gate passes only when it\n   observes every owner. The missing source-order result fails that\n   gate with or without the three assertions.\n   a. From the sealed evidence, with no new run, report the workerd RSS\n      sample nearest the Worker exit and the test files that Worker\n      held. The gate peaked at 3,057,488 KiB of workerd. The version\n      table gate lost a Worker to a heap abort near 3.3 GiB on\n      9 November. If the exit sits at the peak, say so.\n   b. Do not change a pool, a worker count or a deadline now.\n\n3. Next validation, in this order, once:\n   a. The compiler contexts that read the changed test file.\n   b. One focused Native run of two whole owners: the nine-case\n      archive-installed owner and the source-order owner. Sample RSS.\n   c. The three prechecks only if the source after them changed.\n   d. One full gate at the final head.\n\n4. If the full gate again ends with an unhandled Worker exit or an\n   unobserved owner, and no assertion fails, stop and report the two\n   RSS records side by side. I then rule on a split of the Native\n   project. Do not run a third gate without that ruling.\n\nAll failed histories stay. H keeps the slot until 3a is ready. F then\ntakes the slot first.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}